# Bug Report

TypeScript 4.3 added `--noImplicitOverride` and quick fixes to add an override modifier where it's missing. If the `override` modifier is missing from an abstract method, the quick fix adds it _before_ the `abstract` modifier. This leads to another error: "'abstract' modifier must precede 'override' modifier.(1029)".

### 🔎 Search Terms

override, quick fix, abstract

### 🕗 Version & Regression Information

Tested in playground with TypeScript version 4.3.5 and 4.4.0-beta.

### ⏯ Playground Link

[Playground link with relevant code (4.3.5)](https://www.typescriptlang.org/play?noImplicitOverride=true&ts=4.3.5#code/MYGwhgzhAEAKYCcCmA7ALtA3gKGtAZgPaEAUAlFgL7bXZgBGEaCYwGokMAwgBYCWIACbQkADzSpBMeMnRZc0BkxZsCxcgC5oAN0J9BAbhpA)

[Playground link with relevant code (4.4.0-beta)](https://www.typescriptlang.org/play?noImplicitOverride=true&ts=4.4.0-beta#code/MYGwhgzhAEAKYCcCmA7ALtA3gKGtAZgPaEAUAlFgL7bXZgBGEaCYwGokMAwgBYCWIACbQkADzSpBMeMnRZc0BkxZsCxcgC5oAN0J9BAbhpA)

### 💻 Code

If you apply the quick fix "Add 'override' modifier" to this code ...

```ts
class Parent {
  foo() {}
}

abstract class Child extends Parent {
  abstract foo(): void;
}
```

### 🙁 Actual behavior

... it gets corrected to:

```ts
abstract class Child extends Parent {
  override abstract foo(): void;
}
```

### 🙂 Expected behavior

but it should be:

```ts
abstract class Child extends Parent {
  abstract override foo(): void;
}
```

